---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { data, names, format, mutations } from "../lib/data.js";
const baseline = data.groups.filter(
  (g) => g.scenario === "nq-100k" && g.operation === "insert",
);
---

<Base>
  <section class="intro wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">An open benchmark for vector databases</p>
    <h1>
      When does a change
      <br class="desktop-break" /> become searchable?
    </h1>
    <p class="intro-text">
      Saving a document is only part of the story. We measure how soon inserts,
      replacements, and deletions show up in reads and search results while
      other queries are running.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/results/">
        Explore the results <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="/methodology/">
        Understand the benchmark
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="scope-line">
      Qdrant, Weaviate, and pgvector · Protocol 2 · Release 0.5.0
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="fact-band">
    <dl class="wrap facts">
      <div>
        <dt>{data.completed}</dt>
        <dd>completed trials</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>{mutations.toLocaleString("en-US")}</dt>
        <dd>document changes</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>{Object.keys(data.experiment.datasets).length}</dt>
        <dd>real retrieval datasets</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>100k</dt>
        <dd>largest base collection</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <section class="wrap section overview-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
      <h2>
        Compare one workload
        <br /> at a time.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Choose a collection size and a type of change. Then compare the time
        each database took to show the new state.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every result includes reliability and search quality, so speed has
        context.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/results/">
        Choose a workload →
      </a>
    </div>
    <div class="preview-result">
      <div class="preview-heading">
        <h3>A first look</h3>
        <p>Insert · 100k Wikipedia documents · steady traffic</p>
      </div>
      <div class="preview-label">
        <span>Database</span>
        <span>First visible, p95</span>
      </div>
      {baseline.map((g) => (
        <a
          href={`/results/?scenario=nq-100k&operation=insert#comparison`}
          class="preview-row"
        >
          <strong>{names[g.backend]}</strong>
          <span>
            {format(g.first_p95)} <small>ms</small>
          </span>
        </a>
      ))}
      <p class="small-note">
        Lower is faster. Median of five trial p95s, for successfully confirmed
        changes. <a href="/methodology/#reading-results">What does p95 mean?</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">The idea in one minute</p>
      <h2>Write. Observe. Confirm.</h2>
      <p>
        We look at what an application can actually see through the database
        APIs.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <span class="step-number">1</span>
        <h3>Send a change</h3>
        <p>Add a document, replace an existing document, or delete one.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="step-number">2</span>
        <h3>Read and search</h3>
        <p>
          Independent readers check the document directly and through vector
          search.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="step-number">3</span>
        <h3>Confirm the state</h3>
        <p>
          Both read channels need repeated correct responses spanning at least
          50 milliseconds.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="wrap section bottom-section">
    <div class="reading-callout">
      <h2>A useful reference, with a clear scope.</h2>
      <p>
        These measurements come from one Apple M4 host running pinned Docker
        containers. They include client, network, and database time. Static
        datasets supply real text and questions; the changes are simulated.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use the results to understand this setup, then repeat the protocol on
        the hardware and workload you care about.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="text-link" href="/methodology/">
          Read the method and limitations →
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/reproduce/">
          Run it yourself →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <script>
    // Keep previously shared hash URLs useful after the move to normal Astro pages.
    const old = location.hash.slice(1);
    const [page, query] = old.split("?");
    if (["results", "methodology", "datasets", "reproduce"].includes(page))
      location.replace("/" + page + "/" + (query ? "?" + query : ""));
  </script>
</Base>
